// A gap belongs to the placement, not to the box at either end of it.
//
// The benchmark exercises one asymmetric wedge and nothing else, so this file
// carries the rest: a node-wide default with one placement overriding it, a
// bracket on each of two opposing placements, and contact written as a gap of
// none on a node whose other placement keeps its distance.

diagram background: #111111

style plain  fill: #191728  stroke: #4f5367

box left_wall  "Left wall"   style: plain
box right_wall "Right wall"  right of left_wall  style: plain

// Both sides bind, and they want different distances. Without a gap of its own
// per placement there is one number for both, and the corridor is symmetric
// whether or not the picture wants it to be.
box wedge "Wedged tight left, wide right"  right of left_wall (gap: tight)  left of right_wall (gap: wide)  level with left_wall  style: plain

// `gap:` on the node is still the default for whatever does not say. Here the
// stack sits wide below the wedge and tight to the right of the left wall.
box stack "Node default is wide"  below wedge  right of left_wall (gap: tight)  gap: wide  style: plain

// A gap of none is contact, and it is now sayable on one placement while the
// other keeps its distance — which the node-wide attribute could not do.
box shelf "Flat on the stack"  below stack (gap: none)  right of left_wall (gap: tight)  style: plain

link left_wall -> wedge  from: right  to: left
link wedge -> right_wall  from: right  to: left

// A node's `gap:` reaches the placements written *against* it as well as its
// own. `island` names nothing and states wide; both neighbours are held off at
// that distance, which is what lets an author push a box away from what is
// crowding it without first working out which line happens to mention which.
//
// `west` asks for tight and gets wide, because both ends stated something and a
// gap is a minimum, so the larger of the two is the one that holds.
box island "States wide, names nobody"  below shelf  gap: wide  style: plain
box east   "Takes the island's wide"    right of island  level with island  style: plain
box west   "Asks tight, gets wide"      left of island   level with island  gap: tight  style: plain
